        "original_id": "d2516c2b-23ec-513b-a82c-69fbf1cf0cab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pedro Yanowitz, Hayley Westenra\n- Bands: Shihad, Morningwood\n- Companies: Capitol Records\n- Albums: The General Electric\n- Topics: chart achievements, recording career, band roles\n\nFacts:\n- In October 1999, Shihad released The General Electric as the band's fourth album.\n- During their recording career, Shihad produced five number-one studio albums in New Zealand.\n- Shihad hold the record for the most number-one records by any New Zealand artist alongside Hayley Westenra.\n- Shihad also had three top-ten singles in New Zealand.\n- Morningwood was signed to Capitol Records.\n- Morningwood released two albums.\n- Pedro Yanowitz was the bass player, songwriter, and producer for Morningwood.",
